\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Lord, that I may learn of Thee,
\par Give me true simplicity;
\par Wean my soul, and keep it low,
\par Willing Thee alone to know.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Let me cast my self aside,
\par All that feeds my knowing pride,
\par Not to man, but God submit,
\par Lay my reasonings at Thy feet;
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Of my boasted wisdom spoiled,
\par Docile, helpless, as a child,
\par Only seeing in Thy light,
\par Only walking in Thy might.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Then infuse the teaching grace,
\par Spirit of truth and righteousness;
\par Knowledge, love divine, impart,
\par Life eternal, to my heart.
\par Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

